# Django Models — Padrões (Django 6.x)

## Estrutura canónica

```python
class Post(models.Model):
    class Status(models.TextChoices):       # 1. Choices
        DRAFT = 'draft', 'Draft'
        PUBLISHED = 'published', 'Published'

    title  = models.CharField(max_length=250)            # 2. Campos
    author = models.ForeignKey(
        settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL,
        on_delete=models.CASCADE,
        related_name='blog_posts',
    )
    status = models.CharField(max_length=10, choices=Status, default=Status.DRAFT)

    objects   = models.Manager()            # 3. Managers — objects SEMPRE primeiro
    published = PublishedManager()

    class Meta:                             # 4. Meta
        ordering = ['-publish']
        indexes  = [models.Index(fields=['-publish'])]

    def __str__(self): return self.title    # 5. __str__

    def get_absolute_url(self): ...         # 6. get_absolute_url
```

## Managers customizados

```python
class PublishedManager(models.Manager):    # definir FORA do model
    def get_queryset(self):
        return super().get_queryset().filter(status='published')
```

Omitir `objects = models.Manager()` quando há managers adicionais remove o manager padrão — `Post.objects.all()` falha.

## Meta — regras

```python
class Meta:
    ordering    = ['-publish']                             # lista, não tuplo
    indexes     = [models.Index(fields=['id', 'slug'])]   # não index_together
    constraints = [
        models.UniqueConstraint(fields=['user', 'post'], name='unique_bookmark'),
    ]                                                      # não unique_together
```

## ForeignKey / relações

```python
author = models.ForeignKey(
    settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL,   # nunca User directamente
    on_delete=models.CASCADE,   # obrigatório
    related_name='blog_posts',  # sempre explícito
)

# Models abstractos — %(class)s evita colisões de related_name
class ItemBase(models.Model):
    owner = models.ForeignKey(User, related_name='%(class)s_related', on_delete=models.CASCADE)
    class Meta:
        abstract = True
```

## Campos — regras rápidas

| Campo | Regra |
|---|---|
| Preços | `DecimalField(max_digits=10, decimal_places=2)` — nunca `CharField` |
| Texto opcional | `TextField(blank=True)` — nunca `null=True` em `CharField`/`TextField` |
| Booleano nullable | `BooleanField(null=True)` — nunca `NullBooleanField` |
| Timestamps | `auto_now_add=True` (created), `auto_now=True` (updated) |
| Slug auto | override `save()`: `if not self.slug: self.slug = slugify(self.title)` |

## django-parler (myshop)

```python
class Product(TranslatableModel):
    translations = TranslatedFields(      # nome exacto 'translations' — sem typos
        name=models.CharField(max_length=200),
        slug=models.SlugField(max_length=200),
    )
```

**Filtros ORM com parler:**
```python
Product.objects.filter(translations__slug=slug, available=True)   # CORRECTO
Product.objects.filter(slug=slug)                                  # FieldError
```

**Aceder/escrever em código Python:**
```python
product.set_current_language('en')
product.name = 'New Name'
product.save()
```

**Settings obrigatório** (evita `DoesNotExist` quando falta tradução):
```python
PARLER_LANGUAGES = {
    None: ({'code': 'en'}, {'code': 'es'}),
    'default': {'fallback': 'en', 'hide_untranslated': False},
}
```

## Queries ORM — N+1

```python
# FK/OneToOne → select_related (1 query com JOIN)
Post.published.select_related('author')

# M2M / reverse FK → prefetch_related (2 queries)
Post.published.prefetch_related('tags', 'comments')

# parler → prefetch_related('translations')
Product.objects.prefetch_related('translations').filter(available=True)

# Contagem → annotate, não Python; existência → exists(), não count() > 0
posts = Post.published.annotate(total_comments=Count('comments'))
Bookmark.objects.filter(user=request.user, post=post).exists()
```

## Signals — estrutura e critério

```python
# blog/signals.py
@receiver(post_save, sender=Bookmark)
def bookmark_created(sender, instance, created, **kwargs):
    if created: pass

# blog/apps.py — importar DENTRO de ready(), nunca no topo do módulo
class BlogConfig(AppConfig):
    def ready(self):
        import blog.signals  # noqa: F401
```

| Situação | Abordagem |
|---|---|
| Lógica no mesmo modelo | Override `save()` |
| Efeito secundário desacoplado | Signal |
| Slug auto / campo calculado | Override `save()` |
| Notificar outra app/sistema | Signal |
